const FILM_MD="# Lybi C18 — Film script and production brief\n\nInternal production material, not a finished film or a live demonstration. The first and third beats restore the category anchors. Timing remains indicative and requires a recorded read. The example beat is unapproved source material for refinement; it is not restored to the public page.\n\n## 00–14 s · Capability is not yet a customer decision\n\n**Voice-over:** Agentic AI expands how systems reason, plan and execute. Growth depends on how customers decide—and whether they act.\n\n**Visual direction:** Open with coordinated system work, then the customer’s decision. No performance counters or claims that agentic AI only reduces costs.\n\n**Purpose:** Retain the accepted business rationale without a long technical introduction.\n\n## 14–28 s · The human decision\n\n**Voice-over:** A process can be on track while a customer remains unsure. Priorities, concerns and practical constraints can change what they need before they move forward.\n\n**Visual direction:** Show the process progressing while a relevant question is unresolved. Do not depict emotions as facts read from a face.\n\n**Purpose:** Explain why the decision needs attention before introducing the intelligence.\n\n## 28–44 s · Introducing Conative AI\n\n**Voice-over:** Conative AI is a new layer of intelligence built around the human decision. Lybi models what shapes that decision and directs the work that helps people decide and act.\n\n**Visual direction:** Show Discovery, Value and Conditions shaping an interaction. Value draws on products, services and support, not only price or product terms. Show personal readiness and outstanding organizational requirements separately; the path develops through the interactions.\n\n**Purpose:** State the differentiating mechanism, not a generic promise to persuade.\n\n## 44–64 s · Make the change visible\n\n**Voice-over:** One question reveals a deposit about to mature. A bridge becomes an option to assess. Another question reveals a dollar payment—and the comparison changes again. What the engine learns changes what happens next.\n\n**Visual direction:** Show Lybi’s timing question, Ido’s answer and the stated priority to keep the deposit intact and the working hypothesis beside what was previously known. A possible bridge is retained after dollar payment is discovered; the comparison adds currency and total cost. Distinguish evidence already gathered, current work and the planned next interaction. No approved or cheaper financing is shown. A preference for an option does not imply that bank approval has been obtained.\n\n**Purpose:** Give the viewer a visible turning point, not another recitation of the thesis.\n\n## 64–82 s · A complete product\n\n**Voice-over:** Built-in professional expertise, agentic execution and enterprise controls put that intelligence to work. Your objectives and boundaries guide the system. Your customer makes the decision.\n\n**Visual direction:** Pull back to the complete product: Conative Engine, ready domain expertise, operation and controls. The ready journey contains professional methods; each customer’s path develops individually. Close on Lybi and one invitation to explore the application.\n\n**Purpose:** End on what the organization receives and the customer’s agency.\n\n## Permanent close\n\nWhere your AI investment meets the top line.\n\nProduct invitation: explore a ready Decision Journey, its fit, launch and measurement. Do not close on a blank agent-building exercise.\n\nNo timing, quantified business impact, clinical result or independent approval is established by this script. Source definitions and two-sided Conditions remain governed by the current website brief.\n";
